	'messages:apihelp-compare-param-toslots' => 'en:Override content of the revision specified by <var>totitle</var>, <var>toid</var> or <var>torev</var>.

This parameter specifies the slots that are to be modified. Use <var>totext-&#x7B;slot}</var>, <var>tocontentmodel-&#x7B;slot}</var>, and <var>tocontentformat-&#x7B;slot}</var> to specify content for each slot.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-extended-description' => 'en:See the various prop-modules of <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query|action=query]]</kbd> to get information from the current version of a page.

There are several ways to specify the text to parse:
# Specify a page or revision, using <var>$1page</var>, <var>$1pageid</var>, or <var>$1oldid</var>.
# Specify content explicitly, using <var>$1text</var>, <var>$1title</var>, <var>$1revid</var>, and <var>$1contentmodel</var>.
# Specify only a summary to parse. <var>$1prop</var> should be given an empty value.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-usearticle' => 'en:Use the ArticleParserOptions hook to ensure the options used match those used for article page views',
	'messages:apihelp-query+alldeletedrevisions-param-miser-user-namespace' => 'en:<strong>Note:</strong> Due to [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Manual:$wgMiserMode|miser mode]], using <var>$1user</var> and <var>$1namespace</var> together may result in fewer than <var>$1limit</var> results returned before continuing; in extreme cases, zero results may be returned.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+filerepoinfo-paramvalue-prop-articlepath' => 'en:Repository wiki\'s <var>[[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Manual:$wgArticlePath|$wgArticlePath]]</var> or equivalent.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+filerepoinfo-paramvalue-prop-server' => 'en:Repository wiki\'s <var>[[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Manual:$wgServer|$wgServer]]</var> or equivalent.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+langlinks-example-simple' => 'en:Get interlanguage links from the page [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]].',
	'messages:apihelp-query+links-example-namespaces' => 'en:Get links from the page [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]] in the {{ns:user}} and {{ns:template}} namespaces.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+logevents-param-action' => 'en:Filter log actions to only this action. Overrides <var>$1type</var>. In the list of possible values, values with the asterisk wildcard such as <kbd>action/*</kbd> can have different strings after the slash (/).',
	'messages:apihelp-query+pageprops-param-prop' => 'en:Only list these page properties (<kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+pagepropnames|action=query&list=pagepropnames]]</kbd> returns page property names in use). Useful for checking whether pages use a certain page property.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+pageswithprop-param-propname' => 'en:Page property for which to enumerate pages (<kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+pagepropnames|action=query&list=pagepropnames]]</kbd> returns page property names in use).',
	'messages:apihelp-query+prefixsearch-extended-description' => 'en:Despite the similarity in names, this module is not intended to be equivalent to [[Special:PrefixIndex]]; for that, see <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+allpages|action=query&list=allpages]]</kbd> with the <kbd>apprefix</kbd> parameter. The purpose of this module is similar to <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/opensearch|action=opensearch]]</kbd>: to take user input and provide the best-matching titles. Depending on the search engine backend, this might include typo correction, redirect avoidance, or other heuristics.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+random-extended-description' => 'en:Pages are listed in a fixed sequence, only the starting point is random. This means that if, for example, <samp>Main Page</samp> is the first random page in the list, <samp>List of fictional monkeys</samp> will <em>always</em> be second, <samp>List of people on stamps of Vanuatu</samp> third, etc.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+recentchanges-paramvalue-prop-userid' => 'en:Adds the user ID responsible for the edit. If the user has been revision deleted, a <samp>userhidden</samp> property will be returned.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+recentchanges-paramvalue-prop-parsedcomment' => 'en:Adds the parsed comment for the edit. If the comment has been revision deleted, a <samp>commenthidden</samp> property will be returned.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+revisions-extended-description' => 'en:May be used in several ways:
# Get data about a set of pages (last revision), by setting titles or pageids.
# Get revisions for one given page, by using titles or pageids with start, end, or limit.
# Get data about a set of revisions by setting their IDs with revids.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+revisions+base-paramvalue-prop-parsetree' => 'en:Use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/expandtemplates|action=expandtemplates]]</kbd> or <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/parse|action=parse]]</kbd> instead. The XML parse tree of revision content (requires content model <code>$1</code>). For performance reasons, if this option is used, <var>$3limit</var> is enforced to $2.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+revisions+base-param-slots' => 'en:Which revision slots to return data for, when slot-related properties are included in <var>$1props</var>. If omitted, data from the <kbd>main</kbd> slot will be returned in a backwards-compatible format.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+revisions+base-param-expandtemplates' => 'en:Use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/expandtemplates|action=expandtemplates]]</kbd> instead. Expand templates in revision content (requires $1prop=content).',
	'messages:apihelp-query+revisions+base-param-generatexml' => 'en:Use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/expandtemplates|action=expandtemplates]]</kbd> or <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/parse|action=parse]]</kbd> instead. Generate XML parse tree for revision content (requires $1prop=content).',
	'messages:apihelp-query+revisions+base-param-parse' => 'en:Use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/parse|action=parse]]</kbd> instead. Parse revision content (requires <var>$2prop=content</var>). For performance reasons, if this option is used, <var>$2limit</var> is enforced to $1.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+revisions+base-param-diffto' => 'en:Use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/compare|action=compare]]</kbd> instead. Revision ID to diff each revision to. Use <kbd>prev</kbd>, <kbd>next</kbd> and <kbd>cur</kbd> for the previous, next and current revision respectively. For performance reasons, if this option is used, <var>$2limit</var> is enforced to $1.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+revisions+base-param-difftotext' => 'en:Use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/compare|action=compare]]</kbd> instead. Text to diff each revision to. Only diffs a limited number of revisions. Overrides <var>$2diffto</var>. If <var>$2section</var> is set, only that section will be diffed against this text. For performance reasons, if this option is used, <var>$2limit</var> is enforced to $1.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+revisions+base-param-contentformat' => 'en:Serialization format used for <var>$1difftotext</var> and expected for output of content.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+siteinfo-paramvalue-prop-showhooks' => 'en:Returns a list of all subscribed hooks (contents of <var>[[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Manual:$wgHooks|$wgHooks]]</var>).',
	'messages:apihelp-query+tokens-summary' => 'en:Gets tokens for data-modifying actions.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+transcludedin-param-show' => 'en:Show only items that meet these criteria:',
	'messages:apihelp-query+transcludedin-paramvalue-show-!redirect' => 'en:Only show non-redirects.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+usercontribs-param-show' => 'en:Show only items that meet these criteria, e.g. non minor edits only: <kbd>$2show=!minor</kbd>.

If <kbd>$2show=patrolled</kbd> or <kbd>$2show=!patrolled</kbd> is set, revisions older than <var>[[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Manual:$wgRCMaxAge|$wgRCMaxAge]]</var> ($1 {{PLURAL:$1|second|seconds}}) won\'t be shown.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+userinfo-paramvalue-prop-groupmemberships' => 'en:Lists groups that the current user has been explicitly assigned to, including the expiry date of each group membership.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+userinfo-paramvalue-prop-theoreticalratelimits' => 'en:Lists all rate limits that would apply to the current user if they were not exempt from all ratelimits based on user rights or ip.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+userinfo-paramvalue-prop-acceptlang' => 'en:Echoes the <code>Accept-Language</code> header sent by the client in a structured format.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+userinfo-paramvalue-prop-unreadcount' => 'en:Adds the count of unread pages on the user\'s watchlist (maximum $1; returns <samp>$2</samp> if more).',
	'messages:apihelp-query+userinfo-param-attachedwiki' => 'en:With <kbd>$1prop=centralids</kbd>, indicate whether the user is attached with the wiki identified by this ID.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+users-paramvalue-prop-groupmemberships' => 'en:Lists groups that each user has been explicitly assigned to, including the expiry date of each group membership.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+users-paramvalue-prop-emailable' => 'en:Tags if the user can and wants to receive email through [[Special:Emailuser]].',
	'messages:apihelp-query+users-paramvalue-prop-gender' => 'en:Tags the gender of the user. Returns "male", "female", or "unknown".',
	'messages:apihelp-query+users-paramvalue-prop-centralids' => 'en:Adds the central IDs and attachment status for the user.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+users-param-attachedwiki' => 'en:With <kbd>$1prop=centralids</kbd>, indicate whether the user is attached with the wiki identified by this ID.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-summary' => 'en:Get recent changes to pages in the current user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-param-allrev' => 'en:Include multiple revisions of the same page within given timeframe.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-paramvalue-prop-notificationtimestamp' => 'en:Adds timestamp of when the user was last notified about the edit.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-paramvalue-prop-loginfo' => 'en:Adds log information where appropriate.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-param-show' => 'en:Show only items that meet these criteria. For example, to see only minor edits done by logged-in users, set $1show=minor|!anon.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-param-owner' => 'en:Used along with $1token to access a different user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-param-token' => 'en:A security token (available in the user\'s [[Special:Preferences#mw-prefsection-watchlist|preferences]]) to allow access to another user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-example-simple' => 'en:List the top revision for recently changed pages on the current user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-example-props' => 'en:Fetch additional information about the top revision for recently changed pages on the current user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-example-expiry' => 'en:Fetch additional information about the top revision for recently changed pages on the current user\'s watchlist, including when temporarily watched items will expire.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-example-allrev' => 'en:Fetch information about all recent changes to pages on the current user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-example-generator' => 'en:Fetch page info for recently changed pages on the current user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-example-generator-rev' => 'en:Fetch revision info for recent changes to pages on the current user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlist-example-wlowner' => 'en:List the top revision for recently changed pages on the watchlist of user <kbd>Example</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlistraw-paramvalue-prop-changed' => 'en:Adds timestamp of when the user was last notified about the edit.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlistraw-param-show' => 'en:Only list items that meet these criteria.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlistraw-param-owner' => 'en:Used along with $1token to access a different user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-query+watchlistraw-param-token' => 'en:A security token (available in the user\'s [[Special:Preferences#mw-prefsection-watchlist|preferences]]) to allow access to another user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-resetpassword-extended-description-noroutes' => 'en:No password reset routes are available.

Enable routes in <var>[[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Manual:$wgPasswordResetRoutes|$wgPasswordResetRoutes]]</var> to use this module.',
	'messages:apihelp-revisiondelete-example-log' => 'en:Hide all data on log entry <kbd>67890</kbd> with the reason <kbd>BLP violation</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-rollback-extended-description' => 'en:If the last user who edited the page made multiple edits in a row, they will all be rolled back.',
	'messages:apihelp-rollback-param-tags' => 'en:Tags to apply to the rollback.',
	'messages:apihelp-rollback-param-user' => 'en:Name of the user whose edits are to be rolled back.',
	'messages:apihelp-rollback-param-summary' => 'en:Custom edit summary. If empty, default summary will be used.',
	'messages:apihelp-rollback-param-markbot' => 'en:Mark the reverted edits and the revert as bot edits.',
	'messages:apihelp-rollback-param-watchlistexpiry' => 'en:Watchlist expiry timestamp. Omit this parameter entirely to leave the current expiry unchanged.',
	'messages:apihelp-rollback-example-simple' => 'en:Roll back the last edits to page [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]] by user <kbd>Example</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-rollback-example-summary' => 'en:Roll back the last edits to page [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]] by IP user <kbd>192.0.2.5</kbd> with summary <kbd>Reverting vandalism</kbd>, and mark those edits and the revert as bot edits.',
	'messages:apihelp-setnotificationtimestamp-summary' => 'en:Update the notification timestamp for watched pages.',
	'messages:apihelp-setnotificationtimestamp-extended-description' => 'en:This affects the highlighting of changed pages in the watchlist and history, and the sending of email when the "{{int:tog-enotifwatchlistpages}}" preference is enabled.',
	'messages:apihelp-setnotificationtimestamp-param-timestamp' => 'en:Timestamp to which to set the notification timestamp.',
	'messages:apihelp-setnotificationtimestamp-param-torevid' => 'en:Revision to set the notification timestamp to (one page only).',
	'messages:apihelp-setnotificationtimestamp-param-newerthanrevid' => 'en:Revision to set the notification timestamp newer than (one page only).',
	'messages:apihelp-setnotificationtimestamp-example-all' => 'en:Reset the notification status for the entire watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-setnotificationtimestamp-example-page' => 'en:Reset the notification status for [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]].',
	'messages:apihelp-setnotificationtimestamp-example-pagetimestamp' => 'en:Set the notification timestamp for [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]] so all edits since 1 January 2012 are unviewed.',
	'messages:apihelp-setnotificationtimestamp-example-allpages' => 'en:Reset the notification status for pages in the <kbd>{{ns:user}}</kbd> namespace.',
	'messages:apihelp-stashedit-summary' => 'en:Prepare an edit in shared cache.',
	'messages:apihelp-stashedit-extended-description' => 'en:This is intended to be used via AJAX from the edit form to improve the performance of the page save.',
	'messages:apihelp-stashedit-param-contentformat' => 'en:Content serialization format used for the input text.',
	'messages:apihelp-stashedit-param-baserevid' => 'en:Revision ID of the base revision.',
	'messages:apihelp-unblock-param-userid' => 'en:Specify <kbd>$1user=#<var>ID</var></kbd> instead.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-summary' => 'en:Undelete revisions of a deleted page.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-extended-description' => 'en:A list of deleted revisions (including timestamps) can be retrieved through [[Special:ApiHelp/query+deletedrevisions|prop=deletedrevisions]], and a list of deleted file IDs can be retrieved through [[Special:ApiHelp/query+filearchive|list=filearchive]].',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-timestamps' => 'en:Timestamps of the revisions to undelete. If both <var>$1timestamps</var> and <var>$1fileids</var> are empty, all will be undeleted.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-fileids' => 'en:IDs of the file revisions to restore. If both <var>$1timestamps</var> and <var>$1fileids</var> are empty, all will be restored.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-watchlistexpiry' => 'en:Watchlist expiry timestamp. Omit this parameter entirely to leave the current expiry unchanged.',
	'messages:apihelp-unlinkaccount-summary' => 'en:Remove a linked third-party account from the current user.',
	'messages:apihelp-unlinkaccount-example-simple' => 'en:Attempt to remove the current user\'s link for the provider associated with <kbd>FooAuthenticationRequest</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-comment' => 'en:Upload comment. Also used as the initial page text for new files if <var>$1text</var> is not specified.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-watchlistexpiry' => 'en:Watchlist expiry timestamp. Omit this parameter entirely to leave the current expiry unchanged.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-filekey' => 'en:Key that identifies a previous upload that was stashed temporarily.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-stash' => 'en:If set, the server will stash the file temporarily instead of adding it to the repository.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-offset' => 'en:Offset of chunk in bytes.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-chunk' => 'en:Chunk contents.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-async' => 'en:Make potentially large file operations asynchronous when possible.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-expiry' => 'en:Expiry timestamps. May be relative (e.g. <kbd>5 months</kbd> or <kbd>2 weeks</kbd>) or absolute (e.g. <kbd>2014-09-18T12:34:56Z</kbd>). If only one timestamp is set, it will be used for all groups passed to the <var>$1add</var> parameter. Use <kbd>infinite</kbd>, <kbd>indefinite</kbd>, <kbd>infinity</kbd>, or <kbd>never</kbd> for a never-expiring user group.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-watchlistexpiry' => 'en:Watchlist expiry timestamp. Omit this parameter entirely to leave the current expiry unchanged.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-example-user' => 'en:Add user <kbd>FooBot</kbd> to group <kbd>bot</kbd>, and remove from groups <kbd>sysop</kbd> and <kbd>bureaucrat</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-example-userid' => 'en:Add the user with ID <kbd>123</kbd> to group <kbd>bot</kbd>, and remove from groups <kbd>sysop</kbd> and <kbd>bureaucrat</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-example-expiry' => 'en:Add user <kbd>SometimeSysop</kbd> to group <kbd>sysop</kbd> for 1 month.',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-param-title' => 'en:The page to (un)watch. Use <var>$1titles</var> instead.',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-param-expiry' => 'en:Expiry timestamp to be applied to all given pages. Omit this parameter entirely to leave any current expiries unchanged.',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-param-unwatch' => 'en:If set the page will be unwatched rather than watched.',
	'messages:apihelp-format-param-wrappedhtml' => 'en:Return the pretty-printed HTML and associated ResourceLoader modules as a JSON object.',
	'messages:api-format-prettyprint-header-hyperlinked' => 'en:This is the HTML representation of the $1 format. HTML is good for debugging, but is unsuitable for application use.

Specify the <var>format</var> parameter to change the output format. To see the non-HTML representation of the $1 format, set [$3 <kbd>format=$2</kbd>].

See the [[mw:API|complete documentation]], or the [[Special:ApiHelp/main|API help]] for more information.',
	'messages:api-login-fail-aborted' => 'en:Authentication requires user interaction, which is not supported by <kbd>action=login</kbd>. To be able to login with <kbd>action=login</kbd>, see [[Special:BotPasswords]]. To continue using main-account login, see <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/clientlogin|action=clientlogin]]</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-login-fail-aborted-nobotpw' => 'en:Authentication requires user interaction, which is not supported by <kbd>action=login</kbd>. To log in, see <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/clientlogin|action=clientlogin]]</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-login-fail-badsessionprovider' => 'en:Cannot log in when using $1.',
	'messages:api-login-fail-sameorigin' => 'en:Cannot log in when the same-origin policy is not applied.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-generator' => 'en:Get the list of pages to work on by executing the specified query module.

<strong>Note:</strong> Generator parameter names must be prefixed with a "g", see examples.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-redirects-generator' => 'en:Automatically resolve redirects in <var>$1titles</var>, <var>$1pageids</var>, and <var>$1revids</var>, and in pages returned by <var>$1generator</var>.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-redirects-nogenerator' => 'en:Automatically resolve redirects in <var>$1titles</var>, <var>$1pageids</var>, and <var>$1revids</var>.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-converttitles' => 'en:Convert titles to other variants if necessary. Only works if the wiki\'s content language supports variant conversion. Languages that support variant conversion include $1.',
	'messages:api-help-flags' => 'en:',
	'messages:api-help-help-urls' => 'en:',
	'messages:api-help-datatypes-top' => 'en:Input to MediaWiki should be NFC-normalized UTF-8. MediaWiki may attempt to convert other input, but this may cause some operations (such as [[Special:ApiHelp/edit|edits]] with MD5 checks) to fail.

Parameters that take multiple values are normally submitted with the values separated using the pipe character, e.g. <kbd>param=value1|value2</kbd> or <kbd>param=value1%7Cvalue2</kbd>. If a value must contain the pipe character, use U+001F (Unit Separator) as the separator \'\'and\'\' prefix the value with U+001F, e.g. <kbd>param=%1Fvalue1%1Fvalue2</kbd>.

Some parameter types in API requests need further explanation:',
	'messages:api-help-datatype-boolean' => 'en:Boolean parameters work like HTML checkboxes: if the parameter is specified, regardless of value, it is considered true. For a false value, omit the parameter entirely.',
	'messages:api-help-datatype-timestamp' => 'en:Timestamps may be specified in several formats, see [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Timestamp|the Timestamp library input formats documented on mediawiki.org]] for details. ISO 8601 date and time is recommended: <kbd><var>2001</var>-<var>01</var>-<var>15</var>T<var>14</var>:<var>56</var>:<var>00</var>Z</kbd>. Additionally, the string <kbd>now</kbd> may be used to specify the current timestamp.',
	'messages:api-help-templatedparams' => 'en:Templated parameters support cases where an API module needs a value for each value of some other parameter. For example, if there were an API module to request fruit, it might have a parameter <var>fruits</var> to specify which fruits are being requested and a templated parameter <var>{fruit}-quantity</var> to specify how many of each fruit to request. An API client that wants 1 apple, 5 bananas, and 20 strawberries could then make a request like <kbd>fruits=apples|bananas|strawberries&apples-quantity=1&bananas-quantity=5&strawberries-quantity=20</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-help-param-type-expiry' => 'en:Type: {{PLURAL:$1|1=expiry|2=list of expiries}} ([[Special:ApiHelp/main#main/datatype/expiry|details]])',
	'messages:api-help-param-type-presenceboolean' => 'en:Type: boolean ([[Special:ApiHelp/main#main/datatype/boolean|details]])',
	'messages:api-help-paramvalue-direction-newer' => 'en:List oldest first. Note: $1start has to be before $1end.',
	'messages:api-help-paramvalue-direction-older' => 'en:List newest first (default). Note: $1start has to be later than $1end.',
	'messages:api-help-no-extended-description' => 'en:',
	'messages:api-help-authmanager-general-usage' => 'en:The general procedure to use this module is:
# Fetch the fields available from <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+authmanagerinfo|action=query&meta=authmanagerinfo]]</kbd> with <kbd>amirequestsfor=$4</kbd>, and a <kbd>$5</kbd> token from <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+tokens|action=query&meta=tokens]]</kbd>.
# Present the fields to the user, and obtain their submission.
# Post to this module, supplying <var>$1returnurl</var> and any relevant fields.
# Check the <samp>status</samp> in the response.
#* If you received <samp>PASS</samp> or <samp>FAIL</samp>, you\'re done. The operation either succeeded or it didn\'t.
#* If you received <samp>UI</samp>, present the new fields to the user and obtain their submission. Then post to this module with <var>$1continue</var> and the relevant fields set, and repeat step 4.
#* If you received <samp>REDIRECT</samp>, direct the user to the <samp>redirecttarget</samp> and wait for the return to <var>$1returnurl</var>. Then post to this module with <var>$1continue</var> and any fields passed to the return URL, and repeat step 4.
#* If you received <samp>RESTART</samp>, that means the authentication worked but we don\'t have a linked user account. You might treat this as <samp>UI</samp> or as <samp>FAIL</samp>.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-requests' => 'en:Only use these authentication requests, by the <samp>id</samp> returned from <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+authmanagerinfo|action=query&meta=authmanagerinfo]]</kbd> with <kbd>amirequestsfor=$1</kbd> or from a previous response from this module.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-request' => 'en:Use this authentication request, by the <samp>id</samp> returned from <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+authmanagerinfo|action=query&meta=authmanagerinfo]]</kbd> with <kbd>amirequestsfor=$1</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-mergerequestfields' => 'en:Merge field information for all authentication requests into one array.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-preservestate' => 'en:Preserve state from a previous failed login attempt, if possible.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-returnurl' => 'en:Return URL for third-party authentication flows, must be absolute. Either this or <var>$1continue</var> is required.

Upon receiving a <samp>REDIRECT</samp> response, you will typically open a browser or web view to the specified <samp>redirecttarget</samp> URL for a third-party authentication flow. When that completes, the third party will send the browser or web view to this URL. You should extract any query or POST parameters from the URL and pass them as a <var>$1continue</var> request to this API module.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-continue' => 'en:This request is a continuation after an earlier <samp>UI</samp> or <samp>REDIRECT</samp> response. Either this or <var>$1returnurl</var> is required.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-additional-params' => 'en:This module accepts additional parameters depending on the available authentication requests. Use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+authmanagerinfo|action=query&meta=authmanagerinfo]]</kbd> with <kbd>amirequestsfor=$1</kbd> (or a previous response from this module, if applicable) to determine the requests available and the fields that they use.',
	'messages:apierror-allimages-redirect' => 'en:Use <kbd>gaifilterredir=nonredirects</kbd> instead of <var>redirects</var> when using <kbd>allimages</kbd> as a generator.',
